You are a code reviewer. Working dir: /tmp/hzt-3388928427/bench-run-xs5pps5q/clone/.harness/worktrees/orch-VocanicZ_bench-run-20261115-medium-harness-harness-r05-p1 (a Python package `stockroom` under src/, tests under tests/). Do NOT modify any file in the repo; do scratch work only under a fresh `mktemp -d` dir. Do not run the full unittest suite (someone else runs it). Never kill processes by pattern.

Spec: `brief.md` in the repo is the original request (top authority). PRD with binding decisions: run `gh issue view 1 -R VocanicZ/bench-run-20261115-medium-harness-harness-r05 --json body -q .body` — read its "Implementation Decisions" and "Acceptance criteria" sections. Where the PRD conflicts with brief.md, brief.md wins.

Task:
1. Read all source under src/stockroom and judge it against EVERY acceptance criterion in the PRD and every rule in brief.md. Check correctness and edge cases: parsing rules (SKU/price/reorder/tax/date/quantity regexes, ASCII-only digits, Unicode digits, `1_000`, impossible dates, duplicates), count order & never-below-zero, pricing (half-up rounding, 5%/10% tiers, £500 threshold, largest-remainder penny allocation with ties, per-line tax, no `-0.00`), fulfil availability incl. later movements and status logic, invoice on shipped qty, report sorting & csv/json formats, which files each command reads, exit codes 0/1/2, nothing on stdout on non-zero exit, append byte-exactness (missing trailing newline, file creation, refusal leaves bytes identical), `--dir` anywhere / `--dir=X`, option abbreviations rejected, broken pipe. Run the CLI as `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m stockroom --dir <tmp> ...` against crafted files in temp dirs to verify — verify the brief's examples (stock output, quote SO-1001 total 177.27).
2. PROBE — run this fixed robustness checklist against the real CLI and report EVERY result (pass or fail) with the exact command:
   - a value starting with a dash, positional and as option value: e.g. `history -x`, `history -`, `quote -`, `--dir -x`, `--dir --json`, `report --format -x`, `receive 2024-03-10 AB-100 -5`, `receive 2024-03-10 AB-100 5 -note`, `receive ... 5 --json`, `fulfil - 2024-03-10`;
   - output piped into `head -1` (`stock | head -1`, `report | head -1`, with a large catalogue too, e.g. 20000 products) — must print no traceback/error, exit 0 (check PIPESTATUS);
   - UTF-8 BOM at start of each of the three files;
   - CRLF and lone-CR line endings in each file (lone CR must NOT split lines);
   - a form feed (U+000C) and U+2028 inside a field (name, note, customer) — must not split lines; check how they appear in output and whether the line is accepted/rejected sensibly;
   - also: non-UTF-8 bytes, catalogue path being a directory, empty files, very long lines, note with embedded tab.
3. Report: a list of findings, each with severity, exact reproduction command, observed vs expected, and which criterion/brief rule it relates to. Separately list which acceptance criteria are MET vs UNMET with brief justification. Be terse. Distinguish genuine bugs from style nits.

